  "instruction_steps": [
    {
      "step_number": 1,
      "instruction": "You can use chicken broth in place of the chicken bouillon powder. Add 1/4 cup of broth followed by 2 teaspoons of cornstarch dissolved in 1 tablespoPrepare the tomatoes:",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "abd9dfa6-9630-536c-8f56-e65c319b6a4c",
        "b83e2c18-e9f1-52e7-8c54-258c5112a6af"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 2,
      "instruction": "Slice the tomatoes in half. Remove the tough stem from each half that connects to the vine. Cut each half into equal thirds (you’ll get 6 slices from each tomato).",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "abd9dfa6-9630-536c-8f56-e65c319b6a4c"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 3,
      "instruction": "Make the soft scrambled eggs:",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "9aed9fd1-4d4b-5e37-9554-bdbb001013d5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 4,
      "instruction": "In a cold, 8 to 10-inch nonstick skillet, add the vegetable oil and beaten eggs. Turn the heat to medium. Once a thin layer of eggs is just beginning to cook on the bottom, push the eggs in one direction to create layers of scrambled eggs.",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "15d942b9-3a2a-5c47-b923-9e9244ffae9b",
        "9aed9fd1-4d4b-5e37-9554-bdbb001013d5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 5,
      "instruction": "Cook, gently stirring the whole time, until the scramble eggs are mostly set but still slightly wet and shiny, 2 to 5 minutes. Remove the eggs to a plate and, if needed, wipe out the pan.",
      "timer_seconds": 300,
      "ingredients_used": [
        "9aed9fd1-4d4b-5e37-9554-bdbb001013d5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 6,
      "instruction": "Stir-fry the tomatoes and seasonings:",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "abd9dfa6-9630-536c-8f56-e65c319b6a4c"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 7,
      "instruction": "Add the sesame oil to the pan followed by the tomatoes and stir-fry over medium heat until the tomatoes are softened but not mushy, about 3 minutes. Add the chicken bouillon powder, sugar, and white pepper. Toss until combined and the sugar and bouillon have dissolved, about 1 minute.",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "abd9dfa6-9630-536c-8f56-e65c319b6a4c",
        "b83e2c18-e9f1-52e7-8c54-258c5112a6af",
        "f270ec55-129c-5992-95c5-f18e28e47f62",
        "16d57b2f-588d-5f4a-ba53-79303355e3c7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 8,
      "instruction": "Add eggs, stir-fry, and garnish:",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "9aed9fd1-4d4b-5e37-9554-bdbb001013d5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 9,
      "instruction": "Add the eggs back to the pan with the tomatoes. Stir-fry for about 2 minutes to heat through and combine. Taste, adding salt only if needed. Sprinkle with the green onions and serve with steamed rice.on of water, plus salt to taste.",
      "timer_seconds": 120,
      "ingredients_used": [
        "abd9dfa6-9630-536c-8f56-e65c319b6a4c",
        "9aed9fd1-4d4b-5e37-9554-bdbb001013d5",
